NAME
       head - print the first lines of a file

SYNOPSIS
       head [-n lines] [-c bytes] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
       Writes the first 10 lines of each FILE to standard output. With
       no FILE, or with - as FILE, standard input is read.

OPTIONS
       -c N   print the first N bytes instead of lines
       -n N   print the first N lines (default 10)
       -N     shorthand for -n N

SEE ALSO
       tail(1), less(1)
